WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.776 --> 00:00:02.400
- [Narrator] In movies like Carrie,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.650
blood comes by the buckets.

00:00:05.507 --> 00:00:08.559
Perfecting that red gooey
mess took a long time

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:11.079
and several different recipes.

00:00:11.079 --> 00:00:15.246
This is the story of how
fake movie blood is made.

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:22.839
Back before film and TV, a
simple red handkerchief on stage

00:00:22.839 --> 00:00:26.511
symbolized blood, but
it was kind of boring,

00:00:26.511 --> 00:00:28.261
so some theaters upped the ante

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.889
by boiling a bug known
for its red pigment.

00:00:30.889 --> 00:00:35.191
They used the cochineal bug
because it creates red dye.

00:00:35.191 --> 00:00:37.133
When black and white movies came along,

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.636
pigment didn't matter,

00:00:38.636 --> 00:00:42.840
so Hollywood simplified things
by using chocolate syrup.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.496
Then in the 1930s when
black and white movies

00:00:45.496 --> 00:00:48.437
turned to color, Hollywood
needed a new blood trick.

00:00:48.437 --> 00:00:52.181
Enter John Tinegate, a retired
pharmacist living in England.

00:00:52.181 --> 00:00:55.308
He concocted the most
realistic looking blood yet

00:00:55.308 --> 00:00:58.066
called Kensington gore
using a combination of

00:00:58.066 --> 00:01:02.233
mostly golden syrup, food
coloring, corn flour and water.

00:01:03.661 --> 00:01:05.780
The most famous of the
blood recipes though

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.065
comes form a man named Dick Smith.

00:01:08.065 --> 00:01:10.052
He came up with something on par

00:01:10.052 --> 00:01:12.331
with the Julia Child recipe.

00:01:12.331 --> 00:01:15.663
The catch, his recipe was poisonous.

00:01:15.663 --> 00:01:19.710
One ingredient, Kodak Photo-Flo
is deadly when consumed.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.314
So people started replacing
the poison with creamer

00:01:22.314 --> 00:01:25.343
and other items that won't kill you.

00:01:25.343 --> 00:01:27.634
Today a lot of the fake
blood you see on screen

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.451
is computer generated, but
if you want to be legit,

00:01:30.451 --> 00:01:32.721
it should be poison or bugs.

00:01:32.721 --> 00:01:35.388
(intense music)

